framework ReleaseReplan:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

problem P1:
  |
    Review the current PurposeBus candidate again, replan the canonical roadmap,
    execute the resulting plan, and finish a verified release.

premise PR1:
  |
    The current owner instruction explicitly requests review, replanning,
    implementation of the plan, and release. It authorizes necessary local work.
    Exact external destinations, refs, visibility, and maximum writes must still
    be disclosed and bound before an external release transition.

evidence E1:
  |
    On 2026-09-30 local HEAD and refreshed origin/feature/local-mvp are
    2a2b3a68c8f44a4107268e4fd51949106a37d486. origin/main is
    01e36f5f411e8b464a90eabfdd37fe35acbeb200. GitHub reports a public
    mako10k/purposebus repository, no PRs and no releases, and open Issue #1.

evidence E2:
  |
    Current core 65 tests, MCP 14 tests and controller policy 2 tests passed.
    All critical file hashes in release/v1-contract.json match current bytes.
    Beta, RC and v1 preparation are present as uncommitted local work.
    Controller policy is non-runnable, as explicitly documented.

evidence E3:
  |
    The canonical roadmap passes document check. Its remaining publication
    task depends on an owner authorization criterion with no receipt.
    observe-velocity reports incomplete history and no usable selected actuals.
    The current 1p/day declaration is not measured throughput.

premise I1:
  |
    Inference: passing tests and hashes justify retaining the exact candidate
    as a review input, but do not prove release readiness or public install.
    Independent review, immutable artifact readback, isolated installed-package
    verification and exact external authorization are still required.

evidence E4:
  |
    Independent read-only review reproduced implicit Partition resolution to
    /tmp from this repository when GIT_WORK_TREE=/tmp, contradicting FR-001.
    It reproduced parse_duration of 400 digits followed by s returning infinity
    and add_seconds raising an uncaught OverflowError, violating CLI-004.

premise I2:
  |
    The current implementation must resolve the worktree from the actual cwd
    independent of inherited Git context and classify unrepresentable duration
    or timestamps as InvalidInput. These fixes enforce existing requirements;
    they do not alter accepted public schema or state compatibility.

premise A1:
  |
    Alternative: publish the existing dirty tree immediately. Rejected because
    no immutable Git candidate or exact external payload has been frozen.

premise A2:
  |
    Alternative: extend the release with runnable controller lifecycle or remote
    transport. Rejected as a scope change absent an owner requirement revision.

pending U1:
  |
    Independent review findings, reproducible verification in today's tooling,
    public clean installation, and exact GitHub release authorization are open.
    Package registry publication and public Plugin Directory submission have
    no selected destination and cannot be inferred.

decision D1 based_on P1, PR1, E1, E2, E3, E4, I1, I2, A1, A2, U1:
  |
    Keep the current feature/local-mvp worktree, preserve all existing work,
    review against requirements and accepted additive contracts, and add a
    measured release revalidation task before publication in the canonical PERT.
    Gather independent review, verify immutable artifacts and installed-package
    behavior, correct justified current-contract defects if found, and record
    evidence with measured active time. Prepare a concrete GitHub release
    candidate, refs, assets, Japanese review scope and maximum-write proposal.
    Bind owner authorization before the one-executor external transition,
    independently read back refs and downloaded asset hashes, and run an
    isolated clean-install smoke from the actual public release before claiming
    completion. Do not silently widen scope or accept unknown criteria.
